--
N5008 [expr.const] + [temp.inst]/5: a constexpr function template whose
body initialises a local array from a pack expansion and reads it back in a
loop (libstdc++'s __find_uniq_type_in_pack) is folded when required as a
constant: directly, through a wrapping template, as an enable_if default
template argument, and after a prior run-time use queued its body (the
constant evaluator now converts the queued definition under its recorded
template map instead of substituting the parsed body into the caller's
scope).  The constant evaluator executes for-loops, compound assignments,
increments, and constexpr local arrays.
